  The plan is written to [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/plans/2026-10-02-deploys-page.md[39m. It's uncommitted ([38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/[39m is
  gitignored in this repo anyway). I haven't started implementing, as you asked.

  [1mThe plan in brief[0m

  - [1mTask 1: page renderer.[0m A new [38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m with [38;5;153mrenderDeploys(snapshot, query)[39m and [38;5;153mformatDuration[39m, plus 11
    rendering tests. These cover the header, the filter, both sorts, the chips, durations, the empty state and fallback
    for unknown query values.
  - [1mTask 2: routing.[0m One [38;5;153mROUTES[39m entry in [38;5;153msrc/server.js[39m and one [38;5;153mNAV[39m entry in [38;5;153msrc/layout.js[39m, plus 3 server tests: the 200
    page, a 503 for a missing [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m and a 503 for malformed JSON. The existing [38;5;153mtry/catch[39m already handles the 503,
    so [38;5;153mhandle()[39m doesn't change.

  [1mThe main design choice:[0m the page is built from the template's component library in [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m ([38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m,
  [38;5;153mselectField[39m, [38;5;153mdataTable[39m, [38;5;153mstatusChip[39m, [38;5;153memptyState[39m), not by copying [38;5;153mservices.js[39m. That file hand-writes its own table,
  select, [38;5;153m.pill[39m chips and HTML escaping. The library already handles sorting, sort links with [38;5;153maria-sort[39m, swapping in the
  empty state, auto-submitting the filter and the four chip colors ([38;5;153mok[39m/[38;5;153mbad[39m/[38;5;153mwarn[39m/[38;5;153minfo[39m). So the new page only validates
  the query and maps deploy fields onto those components. The plan doesn't touch [38;5;153mservices.js[39m or add any CSS.

  [1mThings the spec didn't say, which I decided in the plan[0m (listed under "Decisions this plan makes" so you can change
  them):
  - An unknown [38;5;153msort[39m or [38;5;153mdir[39m falls back on its own. So [38;5;153m?sort=service&dir=bogus[39m sorts by service, newest-to-oldest
    direction (descending), rather than resetting both.
  - The Started column shows the raw ISO timestamp, the same way the Services page shows deploy times.
  - Durations under a minute show as [38;5;153m0m 45s[39m.
